{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Roll</b> — He speaks to the one being warned, meaning: make known to Him your ways, for HaShem works all for the sake of the pure one, and grants his request and fulfills his desire in whatever he asks. And when you roll onto Him, He fills your requests. And also to include beyond the requests of the pure one — meaning, even the wicked will come on the day of disaster, so that he does not harm the pure one."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The word גול ('roll') is taken from the verse itself (Proverbs 16:3, גֹּל אֶל־יְהֹוָה מַעֲשֶׂיךָ); Ibn Ezra reads it as addressed to the pure/righteous person being admonished."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:06.325699831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}